WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000 position:97%
For me, Mathematica is primarily a software with a coherent architecture

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:18.000 position:98%
that allows you to write programs in a variety of ways in modifying, like we say, the programing paradigms,

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:25.000 position:97%
which allows you to go from one way of writing a program to another.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:40.000 position:97%
This is a much unlimited domain, since we can do a variety of things with it, at least in my field [math].

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:55.000 position:97%
My name is Richard Breheret, I am a math teacher in the national education, I have been teaching math in high school for about 20 years.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:13.000 position:80%
Which has led to the installation of webMathematica

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:23.000 position:98%
and the possibility to offer to students via a website all that was possible in math.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:30.000 position:61%
I was led to use Mathematica by chance.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:41.000 position:98%
There were very few software (programs) in the 90s that could do these kinds of things.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:54.000 position:97%
We could integrate in Mathematica program contents from primary schools to high schools,

00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:10.000 position:97%
because Mathematica met the expectations by providing the means to illustrate notions that were taught through those programs.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:25.000 position:98%
For webMathematica, at the beginning, the idea was to offer a set of consistent resources to students

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.000 position:61%
who were not familiar with Mathematica.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:50.000 position:97%
Obviously, the advantage was the ease of programing, of course with some experience.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:03:04.000 position:98%
I was led to develop a web interface in which mathematical expression entry was made in the simplest ways possible,

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:09.000 position:98%
using also the terminology specific to math teaching in France,

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:19.000 position:97%
and to ensure that all the calculation power of Mathematica via webMathematica

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:27.000 position:98%
is made in a totally transparent way to the users of the website.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:40.000 position:98%
In the math teaching context, one of many benefits I have found using Mathematica or webMathematica

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:48.000 position:97%
is the possibility to be able to answer from an algebraic perspective, a formal perspective,

00:03:48.000 --> 00:04:03.000 position:98%
to be able to compare them to a satisfactory answer while knowing that in math you won’t always have only one correct answer.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:07.000 position:84%
The second aspect that seems very important to me also

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:16.000 position:97%
is the fact that not only are we able to obtain clear results that are comprehensible to students,

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:21.000 position:89%
but we are also able to show them in a suitable language.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:39.000 position:97%
The work I did with Mathematica on music was simple research for teachers and learners on the historic construction of musical scales.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:49.000 position:97%
One advantage of using Mathematica is to be able, through this part, to obtain the calculations,

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.000 position:77%
listen to the calculations that are being played,

00:04:51.000 --> 00:05:03.000 position:98%
and finally compare the fractions to auditory parts that are familiar to an occidental ear.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:14.000 position:97%
The benefit is... to do calculations to bring the calculations to less complex numbers

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:23.000 position:97%
that we can convert to sound easily and play in the interface of the Mathematica software.

